Z||000000||V8Dreamer||10-01-2001||03:38 PM||||Every time I press any button other than "off" on the heater/ac controls, the alternator/waterpump belt squeals like he!!  At first I thought maybe it was just he temp change and it was getting colder, so I tightened the he!! out of it and figured it was fixed......well, today I turned the defogger on and there it was again!  I'm now starting to wonder if maybe my alternator is going and for some reason the blower motor makes it work too hard or something....or maybe the belt's just shot now from all that slipping and needs to be replaced.  Any thoughts/suggestions/similar experiences???<P>TIA,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackARROW||10-01-2001||04:44 PM||||If you've tighten the belt, and it still squeals - is it squealing because it's slipping?  If yes, than the belt is too worned out.  If the belt is not slipping, then check your water pump. I've had that problem - the inside seal was gone. Check for leak under it (should leak via the peep hole)!  If no leak, than you can put your hand on it to feel any vibe (don't touch the flipping belt; maybe the seal is slowly going away.  You can FEEL the alt. too if you like that   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Are you sure it's not the blower motor that's squealing?  Don't mind, just asking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Good luck<P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"<p>[This message has been edited by BlackARROW (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
